(4963760, 721856, 32011, '<td valign="top">Nice image, though I think many voters might struggle to recognise what it is (many people don''t ride bicycles).  I like the lighting, and the arrangement of the helmet.  The space above it is too large for my liking, and the border doesn''t really add to the image significantly enough to risk using it in a DPC challenge (many voters dislike it - though I don''t think it warrants any deductions in this instance).</td>', 'Nice image, though I think many voters might struggle to recognise what it is (many people don''t ride bicycles).  I like the lighting, and the arrangement of the helmet.  The space above it is too large for my liking, and the border doesn''t really add to the image significantly enough to risk using it in a DPC challenge (many voters dislike it - though I don''t think it warrants any deductions in this instance).', '2008-09-19 09:34:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(4963770, 721673, 32011, '<td valign="top">Nice image.  It''s nice and sharp... I like the angle too.  The gloves and the green background don''t work for me... I find them both very distracting.  The crop might be a little too tight too, though, I''d have to see the original to be sure.  Well done.</td>', 'Nice image.  It''s nice and sharp... I like the angle too.  The gloves and the green background don''t work for me... I find them both very distracting.  The crop might be a little too tight too, though, I''d have to see the original to be sure.  Well done.', '2008-09-19 09:38:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(4963777, 720759, 32011, '<td valign="top">I don''t know why I like this, but I do.<br/> <br/>Perhaps it''s b/c of its simplicity... minimalist feel.  The padlock has a presence about it, and the image gives it am almost 3 dimensional quality.  I''d like to think that this would be a top 10 finish, but given it the DPC voters deciding, I would be very surprised if it finishes that well.  Anyway, congratulations on an excellent (IMO) image.</td>', 'I don''t know why I like this, but I do. Perhaps it''s b/c of its simplicity... minimalist feel.  The padlock has a presence about it, and the image gives it am almost 3 dimensional quality.  I''d like to think that this would be a top 10 finish, but given it the DPC voters deciding, I would be very surprised if it finishes that well.  Anyway, congratulations on an excellent (IMO) image.', '2008-09-19 09:42:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(4963784, 722191, 32011, '<td valign="top">Nice shot.  I''ve got this in my top 10 for this challenge.  I like the minimalism of it.  I like an image that I''d seriously consider using as a desktop, and this falls into that category.  I would have like to have seen more detail in the area below the light, though, given the basic rules for this challenge, this would not have been possible without overexposing the light.  The border doesn''t work for me... think it would have been stronger without it... but that''s only my opinion.  Well done... I hope this does well.</td>', 'Nice shot.  I''ve got this in my top 10 for this challenge.  I like the minimalism of it.  I like an image that I''d seriously consider using as a desktop, and this falls into that category.  I would have like to have seen more detail in the area below the light, though, given the basic rules for this challenge, this would not have been possible without overexposing the light.  The border doesn''t work for me... think it would have been stronger without it... but that''s only my opinion.  Well done... I hope this does well.', '2008-09-19 09:47:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(4963792, 721290, 32011, '<td valign="top">Very ducking funny.  :)<br/> <br/>This is the top scoring condom photo in this challenge, for me anyway.  The humour element (use of ducks and clever title) did it for me.<br/> <br/>In terms of the photo... it suffers because of the multiple shadows from the multiple light sources, the open wrapper is too dominant/distracting, despite you doing well to place it outside of the DOF... perhaps arranged differenly, it might have worked better (for me... perhaps?).</td>', 'Very ducking funny.  :) This is the top scoring condom photo in this challenge, for me anyway.  The humour element (use of ducks and clever title) did it for me. In terms of the photo... it suffers because of the multiple shadows from the multiple light sources, the open wrapper is too dominant/distracting, despite you doing well to place it outside of the DOF... perhaps arranged differenly, it might have worked better (for me... perhaps?).', '2008-09-19 09:53:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(4963807, 722062, 32011, '<td valign="top">Very red.  I like the composition of this image... the dominance, the therefore, importance it converys/imbues on the extinguisher is impressive.  The image suffers because of the shallow DOF, and perhaps for being a little too red (IMO)... but generally, I quite like this image.  Well done.</td>', 'Very red.  I like the composition of this image... the dominance, the therefore, importance it converys/imbues on the extinguisher is impressive.  The image suffers because of the shallow DOF, and perhaps for being a little too red (IMO)... but generally, I quite like this image.  Well done.', '2008-09-19 09:57:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(4963814, 722189, 97954, '<td valign="top">A like the idea but it would play better with a younger child and its also blurry or out of focus. Should almost always place the focus on the eyes.</td>', 'A like the idea but it would play better with a younger child and its also blurry or out of focus. Should almost always place the focus on the eyes.', '2008-09-19 09:59:59.000000', NULL, 1),
