(4971609, 722012, 30982, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by K10DGuy:</b></div><hr/><i> Hm. I still simply get a feeling of threatening from this, or... if not exactly threatening, like it''s a shot post-accident where the parent is hugging the child out of grief.<br/> <br/>Does nobody else feel that when they look at this shot?</i></td></tr></table> <br/>I can see what you''re saying - to me the concern, apprehension is in the pose/expression of the parent, while the child''s appearance exudes security, warmth, safety.  In that respect, I think this works very well not only for this challenge, but as a metaphor for parenting.  So you''re not the only one who saw something a bit more edgy or unsettled.</td>', 'Originally posted by K10DGuy: Hm. I still simply get a feeling of threatening from this, or... if not exactly threatening, like it''s a shot post-accident where the parent is hugging the child out of grief. Does nobody else feel that when they look at this shot? I can see what you''re saying - to me the concern, apprehension is in the pose/expression of the parent, while the child''s appearance exudes security, warmth, safety.  In that respect, I think this works very well not only for this challenge, but as a metaphor for parenting.  So you''re not the only one who saw something a bit more edgy or unsettled.', '2008-09-24 07:30:52.000000', NULL, 0),
